WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest tonight i
an Emmy Award-winning comedian

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
who's currently
in his 18th season

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:05.472 line:92%
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:08.074 size:88% position:44%
He also stars in the new
comedy series "Kenan,"

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:11.277
which airs Tuesday nights
at 8:30 right here on NBC.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:11.945 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, the fairy cursed
Sleeping Beauty

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:15.615 line:92%
to sleep for a hundred years

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.283 line:92%
Sound like the best curse ever

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:20.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
Until the Prince arrived
to try to awaken

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sleeping Beauty
out of her slumber.

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:25.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Princesses are dumb.
-What?

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:26.493 size:78% position:39% line:92%
When did this happen?

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:29.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Recess. Princesses are out.
Empowerment is in.

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:33.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Will you sing us a song
about that, please?

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:34.934 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-[ Sighs ] Okay. Uh...

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.836 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪ Title Nine ♪♪

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:37.971 size:78% position:39% line:92%
♪♪ You are so fine ♪♪

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:41.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪ Famous for your place
in athletics ♪♪

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:41.975 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Both: Yeah, no.

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.943
-Please welcome back to the show
one of the best.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:46.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
Kenan Thompson.
How are you, Kenan?

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:48.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm good, buddy.
How are you doing?

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:49.749 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I am wonderful

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
and got a little bonus "Kenan"
last night.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:54.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
You did "SNL" on Saturday,
you flew to L.A.,

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:58.358
and then you did the Golde
Globes last night with Maya.

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:02.662
And it just must have been
a delight to be with Maya again.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:03.430 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Absolute best.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:06.066
It was the absolute best, just
being around my sisters again --

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, Tina,
you know, Amy and Maya.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:11.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For those who missed it,
can you tell us a little bit

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the characters
you guys played last night

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:17.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, that is Beverly Jackfrui
on the left

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:21.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Francois Jean-Rudy
on the right.

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:25.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is me.
And I speak French only.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.554 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And we were the winners

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:31.157
of Least, I think, Creative Song
or, like...

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think Least Original.
Maybe Least Original.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Least Original, yes.
Least Original.

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:37.297 line:92%
-It was really fun to see.

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:41.034
It must have, you know --
Obviously it was extremely

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:43.236 size:84% position:42%
difficult circumstances
to do an awards show.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:46.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it was like being
in front of any audience,

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:48.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
like you guys have managed
to do with "SNL."

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:49.809 line:92%
It's still something special

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:50.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's nice to have,
you know,

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:53.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
some people in the room
and not, like, totally virtual

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know, it was
really isolated backstage,

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:58.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I didn't really see
anybody famous.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.052 line:92%
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:01.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
My first time at the Globes,
and I saw just me.

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:02.789 line:92%
It was like, "Okay, well.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:06.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is this the Golden Globes
or is this my house?"

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:09.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm very --
I want to talk about your show

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:12.932
because I'm very jealous about
a famous person on your show

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:13.867 size:78% position:39% line:92%
who I have never met,

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:17.437
and that person is Don Johnson
who is very funny on your show

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:18.571 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And I'm just wondering,

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:22.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
is he a fun person to be aroun
in real life?

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:24.277 line:92%
-Don Johnson is the greatest

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:25.445 line:92%
Like, he could not be nice

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:27.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he could not have
better stories.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:31.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, this guy was in Miam
in the '80s and survived.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:35.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he just loves to laugh
you know,

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:37.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we got really close,
you know,

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:39.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
over our FaceTime meeting
when I first met him.

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:42.896
You know, we just had, you know,
just similar energy.

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:45.965
I don't know how to explain it
He's just a nice guy, you know

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:49.169
And I've been a fan of him
you know, since those days

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:51.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was a little kid,
but I knew he was cool,

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:53.506
and to find out that he's cool
in real life was just great.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:56.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, 'cause they were --
I forget that they, of course,

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:57.644 line:92%
were shooting "Miami" for Miami,

00:02:57.644 --> 00:02:59.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
and if you were
a fan of that show,

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
that meant you were
a certain kind of person

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:03.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
who probably wanted to hang ou
with Don Johnson.

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:06.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you either like Ferrari
or you like guns

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:10.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
or you like blazers
with colorful undershirts.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.625 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.460 line:92%
-You -- You also returned

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:20.033
one of my favorite character
on "SNL" last week, LaVar Ball

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.067 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh. Crazy.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:23.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You do seem to be
having a genuine ball

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:25.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you are doing
this character.

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:28.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it as much fun as it looks?
-It really is,

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:31.811
and I think that's kind of
my overall approach to "Update,"

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:33.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially when I'm nervou
about something.

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I haven't done LaVar
in a while,

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:38.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's kind of
a niche kind of character.

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:41.120
Like, not a lot of people
know exactly who he is.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.923
So the more energy I give to it,
people can just have fun

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:46.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
with it without even knowing
like, kind of,

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
who I'm talking about
or whatever.

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:49.362 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So, the shoe helps.

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:52.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
The chocolate shoe, the cookie
the caramel in the shoe.

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:54.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, all those
little crazy additives

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:58.271
help everybody enjoy the fac
that there's comedy happenin

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:00.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you should just enjoy it
You know what I mean?

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, because if he wasn'
a real person,

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:06.246
he would also be a fantastic
original character on "Update.

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:09.716 size:84% position:42%
So you guys definitely
make it work both ways.

00:04:09.716 --> 00:04:12.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you very much.
The Cara-mellos!

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:14.687 line:92%
Also put Charlotte on the map.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:17.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
I heard so much from Charlotte
people over the weekend.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:20.159
They were like, "Thank you
for shouting out Gastonia.

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:22.395
-How do you like --
How are you enjoying sitcom life

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:25.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
for being a guy
who didn't just do 18 year

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:27.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
or hasn't just done
18 years of "SNL" sketches

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:30.003 size:81% position:41%
but was doing sketches
for years before that?

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:32.205 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How is sitcom life?

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:33.439 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-It's very different.

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:36.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it's like --
As soon as I come to work,

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:38.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
we start shooting
and we're shooting all day

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:41.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's, like, performance
every day, all day

00:04:41.014 --> 00:04:43.416 size:78% position:39%
as opposed to, like,
"Saturday," you know,

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:44.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
we have writing headaches
or whatever,

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:47.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then, like, rehearsal,
but it's still kind of casual.

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:49.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're in our clothes,
like, our normal clothes

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:52.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
as opposed to hair and makeu
all week, you know?

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:54.694 line:92%
So it's a bit of a grind.

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:56.462 line:92%
I mean, they're both different

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:57.597 line:92%
I think "SNL" is more mental

00:04:57.597 --> 00:05:00.500 size:81% position:41%
and sitcom is probably
a lot more physical.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.401 line:92%
Like, a lot more physical.

00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:03.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have two young daughter
in real life.

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:06.973
Have they come to set yet
to meet your TV daughters?

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:09.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Unfortunately, no,
and they are dying to.

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:10.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
They talk about them
all the time.

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:12.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're, like,
so intrigued by them.

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:15.982
You know, it's like,
"So are they us or are we them?"

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:16.949 line:92%
It's like, "No, sweethearts.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:19.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys are
separate individuals.

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:21.087 size:75% position:38% line:92%
This is television."

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:25.458
But, yeah, my big girl, Georgia,
she's obsessed with the show

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:26.492 line:92%
She thinks it's really cool.

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I guess it's good
that they haven't been abl

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:30.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
to come to set yet,
because sometimes, Kenan,

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:31.964 line:92%
don't take offense to this

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:33.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
you do not behave
the way a father should.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:36.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've been acting up lately.
-Yeah, so, our friend,

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:39.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
Mike O'Brien,
who was a writer at "SNL"

00:05:39.105 --> 00:05:42.375 size:84% position:42%
and now is the creator
of the show "AP Bio" --

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:43.609 line:92%
you stopped by his parking spot?

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:45.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, Kenan,
do you want to explain?

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:46.479 line:92%
-Yeah, I saw his parking spot,

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:48.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I thought
I'd take a little photo.

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:51.217 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:53.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just to show him a little love
-Yeah.

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:56.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, you know, I can't wai
until he sees this.

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:56.989 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:59.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is the first
he'll be seeing it?

00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:00.727 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Absolutely.

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:05.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Kenan, I realized something
right before you came on.

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:09.035 line:92%
This is our 1,111th show.

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:09.702 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
11-11.

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:13.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if memory serves,
you were married 11-11-11.

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:15.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, 1-11 is a big number
for my wife.

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:18.978
She's big on the number 3.
I was big on the number 33

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:20.847 line:92%
So, yeah, 11-11-11 came up

00:06:20.847 --> 00:06:22.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we wanted
to get married on that date.

00:06:22.782 --> 00:06:27.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
My dressing room for the Golde
Globes was 111 yesterday.

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:31.491
And, yeah, it's kind of a thin
that, you know, circulates us.

00:06:31.491 --> 00:06:36.462 size:84% position:42%
I can't believe I'm on
your episode, on 1,111.

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:37.130 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Like, that's incredible.

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:40.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
But congratulations to you
That is so many checks.

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:43.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Whistling ]
-Thank you.

00:06:43.302 --> 00:06:46.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
When somebody told me
it has been 1,111 shows,

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:48.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said,
"Give it to me in checks.

00:06:48.274 --> 00:06:50.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't want to hear
how many shows I've done."

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.612 line:92%
-Count it in checks, please.

00:06:52.612 --> 00:06:54.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, buddy, thanks as alway
for being here.

00:06:54.714 --> 00:06:58.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congrats on all your shows
And great job again last night

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:01.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Man, thank you so very much
It was a great weekend.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.956
It's great to see you as always.
I love you. I miss you.

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:05.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm sure I'll see you soon
-I'll bet.

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:07.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll see you
back in the building.

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:11.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Kenan" airs Tuesdays
